        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A redwood fence is one of the easiest exterior wood projects to keep looking good, because gravity and vertical drainage are on your side. Dry wood, a clean and brightened surface, a penetrating semi-transparent stain worked into every end and both faces, and the right fasteners will carry most fences three years or more between coats.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose clear only if the fence is shaded or you are happy to recoat every year, and choose solid only if the boards are too mismatched to show. For the individual products, our redwood sealer rankings are the next stop.
          </p>
